  "description": "T1-Redwood, extensive surface rooting visible, with lifting and damage to the path and as well as to two paved patio areas.  Suggested works are to carry out root pruning to enable the pathway and paved patio areas to be relaid. For the patio areas, mostly small diameter root pruning required of 2-5cm. For the tarred footpath several larger roots would need to be pruned of 5cm-10cm. All roots to be excavated by hand tools and pruned with sharp, clean saws. Currently the footpath is a trip hazard and needs to be relaid. Exact number and diameter of roots to be pruned can only be accurately specified once all the paving and tar is lifted.\r\nTPO (204/1995)]",
